what is up everybody it's animak here  for anime uproar and today i will be  discussing the heartbreaking aftermath  of the ua trader reveal how this  completely changes the class 1a dynamic  that we used to love and i will talk  about izaba's secret master plan to trap  the villains using the ua trader mha is  in the end game now and deku especially  is carrying a lot of weight if you know  what i mean so let's get into it if you  enjoy our boku no hero videos and you  want us to keep it going do me a quick  favor just leave a like and comment it  only takes a second but it really helps  with the youtube algorithm and if you  want a completely free way to directly  support this channel just take a second  to subscribe hit the bell and then  select the option that says all you  might think that's not a big deal who  cares if one person subscribes but  actually on youtube that means a lot you  can also hit me up on twitter and or  instagram at animeopror this video will  of course contain boku no hero manga  spoilers so please proceed with caution  you have been warned the previous  chapter ended with aoyama and his family  being interrogated by the authorities  and with deku reaching out his hand to  aoyama and telling him that he can still  be a hero the latest chapter is called  the story of how we all became heroes  part 1 and it really focuses on class 1a  and how they are all dealing with the  fact that one of their own was the ua  traitor back in the interrogation room  sansa the kitty cat cop covers ayama's  mouth so that he can't talk as he  continues to cry tsukauchi then  hilariously points out to deku that  aoyama is currently restrained so he  can't take deku's hand i mean obviously  deku's point was mostly symbolic but  it's still funny to see tokauchi  bringing deku back to reality in more  ways than one at the end of the day no  matter how much sympathy deku and the  others might feel for aoyama and his  plight he's still been working with all  for one for years and he directly  assisted in some of his crimes and even  though the cops don't think that aoyama  was rigged with a self-destruction quirk  like lady nagant was they still think  it's better to keep him from talking  just in case something he says ends up  triggering some sort of trap that all  for one has set up honestly this might  seem a bit cruel at first glance because  aoyama is clearly remorseful but not  only was lady nagant booby trapped as  you will recall so was kurogiri he had  been rigged to completely pass out if he  ever started revealing any important  information about the villains so it's  possible that aoyama has some sort of  trigger as well tsukauji then asks  yuga's parents why they never told all  for one about the hero raiden camino  back then the villains were caught by  surprise and as a result all for one had  to emerge out into the open and this  ultimately led to his imprisonment if  the villains had had prior intel about  the raid things could have turned out  very differently the aoyama has  explained that they had no way of  reaching out to offer one at that time  it seems that they can only speak to him  if he reaches out to them first so they  had no way of telling him anything  unless he contacted them directly and  while this might prevent alpha-1 from  getting all of the important info that  he could have wanted in real time it  also protects him from being found out  if the aoyamas are ever discovered this  means that the aoyamas literally have no  way of contacting or locating all for  one it doesn't matter what the police do  to them they could even torture them but  the aoyamas will never be able to  provide any useful intel on all for one  location i mean it's kind of brilliant  to be honest and it's exactly the type  of thing that you would expect from a  criminal mastermind however multiple  members of class 1a believe that they  can still use aoyama and his status as  the ua trader to gain an advantage over  all for one kaminari mineta momo and  others seem ready to forgive aoyama just  like deku or at least they seem to be  willing to give him a chance at  redemption president mike is like okay  hold up and he tries to warn them that  they can't just start trusting aoyama  now after he deceived them for so long  but then even ida jumps in and says that  they have to let bygones be bygones okay  what eda the guy who is known for being  a stickler for the rules who is the  class representative wants to forgive  the ua trader so quickly like it's  nothing the same ua trader who put his  entire class that he is responsible for  in danger multiple times honestly i was  not a fan of this at all i can  understand deku's behavior because  that's kind of who he's always been and  i know that eda has evolved since the  beginning of the series in terms of  always following the rules to the letter  but i still feel that some of the class  1a students are too eager to forgive  aoyama way too quickly i mean i know  that horikoshi wants to give aoyama some  form of redemption and i'm totally fine  with that happening eventually but  shouldn't aoyama's classmates take some  time to actually process their feelings  before just forgiving him on the spot am  i the only one who feels that this is  happening way too quickly i never  thought i'd say this but to me bakugou  sounds like the voice of reason on this  one he says that he's gone through hell  because of aoyama which is true and he  just wants to blow oyama up with like  five howitzer impacts that totally makes  sense he's reacting like a normal person  under the circumstances but then cerro  tells him that he's being too harsh and  kirishima goes on to yell out a bunch of  stuff at aoyama but the gist of what he  yells out is essentially that he also  believes that they can move past this  then aizawa facetimes everyone from the  hospital and he takes full  responsibility for not seeing that one  of his own students was operating as the  ua trader right under his nose but  isabel then goes on to say something  that i really don't know how to feel  about he tells ayama that he has no  intention of expelling him from ua  instead he has devised a plan izawa  proceeds to tell tsukauji to cover up  the ears of the aoyamas so that he can  reveal the plan to the others presumably  this plan will involve aoyama but izawa  doesn't want him to know about the plan  just yet in case all for one still has  some way of extracting information from  him unfortunately we don't get to hear  this secret plan yet although by the  reaction of those in the room who did  hear it it seems to be an intriguing and  very consequential plan according to  nezu it is also a very practical plan  but tsukauji doesn't know if they should  even attempt it at any rate the class 1a  students are told to keep the plan  secret from everyone else and then  aoyama and his family are taken to the  police hq as the students look on also  ochako has her hair tied up so you know  things are about to go down back inside  the dorms the students are trying to  come to terms with everything that  happened and they are also preparing to  execute aizawa's mysterious plan all the  remaining class 1a students pledge to  defeat the villains and they all have  serious and intense looks on their faces  deku has a serious and intense look as  well and since he and ita need new hero  costumes after their current ones were  damaged they head to meet up with the  one and only mei hatsume the full-time  genius inventor and part-time deranged  mad scientist deku knows that in order  to prepare for the next big villain  battle he has to be in top shape and so  does all of his gear and so he maintains  that intense look as he tries to enter  may's workshop but he is suddenly blown  to the ground along with the door after  an intense explosion just randomly goes  off inside the workshop the last page of  the chapter shows mei lying on top of  deku her oppai right in deku's face and  although hida is like what the [ __ ] deku  is still maintaining that same intense  look on his face as mei's oppai pressed  down upon him and that is how this  chapter ends okay okay i'll be real with  you guys i am not a huge fan of this  chapter but that moment where deku is  still maintaining a serious look as  mei's oppai crush his face made me laugh  out loud that is some iron-willed  determination right there this man will  not let anything distract him from his  mission and i respect that that said  though as i mentioned earlier i'm not a  fan of so many students being willing to  forgive aoyama so quickly like yes  bakugou is still holding it down and to  be fair we haven't heard from all the  different students individually but to  have so many students act like aoyama  didn't just put all of them and their  teachers and other people in direct  danger for like a year is just  unrealistic again i can totally  understand if eventually over time they  can come to forgive him after he helps  them fight against the villains and  redeems himself but this just feels  rushed i get that horikoshi is trying to  move the story along but we have to get  a proper emotional progression after  five years of wondering who the ua  trader is i mean how do you guys feel  about this am i overreacting when i say  that this felt rushed and unrealistic or  do you agree with me the most  interesting thing about this chapter to  me is isawa's secret plan which almost  certainly involves aoyama trying to use  his status as the ua traitor to deceive  all for one and the villains when isabel  first said that he's not going to expel  aoyama i thought it was just another  example of people forgiving him way too  easily because it was convenient for the  plot but when aizawa says that he has a  plan and that the aoyamas cannot hear  what that plan is yet i realized that  keeping aoyama at ua and acting like  everything is normal is probably part of  isa's plan to lure the villains into a  trap if they were to expel aoyama now  the villains would immediately know that  the traitor has been compromised but  will this mysterious plan actually work  with all for one being as careful as he  is i guess it all depends on the nature  of eiza's secret plan but i'm very  curious to find out what exactly he has  in mind we know that all for one has  like 10 plans and backup plans going at  the same time so the heroes definitely  do need to put their own plans into  motion before it's too late what do you  guys think isawa's secret plan is and  what exactly will it try to accomplish  is it going to involve using the traitor  to make all for one thing that deku is  out alone somewhere but then it turns  out that it's a trap set by the heroes  will it be something else definitely  share your thoughts down in the comments  below the reveal of the ua trader has  definitely shifted the dynamic between  the class 1a students and they will  probably never be as trusting of each  other as they once were that of course  is to be expected the innocent and naive  class 1a students we once knew are gone  the class 1a students we see now are  becoming battle hardened and experienced  heroes and they have gone through some  truly terrifying and tragic ordeals and  it is for this reason that i hope  horikoshi won't just have everyone  forgive aoyama so easily because after  everything that happened that just  wouldn't make sense give it some time  allow the class to deal with what  happened have aoyama actually do  something to redeem himself and then  let's talk about forgiveness the class  1a students we see today are much more  mature and experienced than the students  we used to know and so their reaction to  the ua trader reveal has to reflect that  i mean people have died cities have been  destroyed and forgiveness must be earned  at least that's my two cents  if you guys enjoyed this video and you  want to see more in the future leave a